WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.271
Week 25: Future, Probability, and Forecasting. make forecasts state commitments express probability about the present

2
00:00:08.271 --> 00:00:15.817
Mission brief. Give a five-year forecast, distinguish evidence from speculation, and commit to two actions.

3
00:00:15.817 --> 00:00:25.435
Preparation. Select ten useful words, three linking expressions, and two repair phrases. Plan points rather than a memorized paragraph.

4
00:00:25.435 --> 00:00:33.451
Performance. Complete the task once for fluency, review the evidence, then repeat it for greater clarity and accuracy.

5
00:00:33.451 --> 00:00:42.191
After-action review. Record what succeeded, what blocked communication, and the single change that will matter most on the next attempt.

6
00:00:42.191 --> 00:01:13.633
Model language. Voy a dar un pronóstico a cinco años. — I am going to give a five-year forecast. Distingo entre evidencia y especulación. — I distinguish between evidence and speculation. Me comprometo a dos acciones concretas. — I commit to two concrete actions. Uso datos medibles cuando puedo. — I use measurable data when I can. Mi pronóstico es razonable, no exagerado. — My forecast is reasonable, not exaggerated.

7
00:01:13.633 --> 00:01:23.787
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
